        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                "word": "pousse-au-jouir",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb055bf6-4340-3080-a2a9-b743104e5fbe",
                        "entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pulsion visant la jouissance et le plaisir."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "acf2767f-6b6c-475c-962d-25f3cc87df0c",
                                "sense_id": "eb055bf6-4340-3080-a2a9-b743104e5fbe",
                                "text": "Ainsi, je dirais, en psychanalyste, que la structure du discours scientifique comporte une forme d’auto-reproduction qui en fait un discours qui jouit de lui-même et entretient un principe de pousse-au-jouir pour lui-même. Le discours scientifique est un discours pulsionnel. Il y a dans le discours de la science une force libidinale qui pousse à l’alimenter toujours plus. Elle est là la raison principale de l’aliénation de l’homme moderne à ce discours."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ec4455f-e1d6-33c4-86a3-ed83f58e086a",
                        "entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne ou groupe de personne mettant en avant l’hédonisme comme principe de vie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07d5290c-5603-472a-80ef-9effc36c9de9",
                                "sense_id": "5ec4455f-e1d6-33c4-86a3-ed83f58e086a",
                                "text": "…dans les médias où l’on constate « la prise de pouvoir des nouveaux pousse-au-jouir » qui prétendent combler les individus."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "554a03ef-052b-482c-aaaf-6c6197867fe4",
                        "source_entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "Lustprinzip",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Lustprinzip",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69f979bd-cb72-3536-9502-1f6d8c55f30c",
                                        "entry_id": "3c39743f-7d68-3a96-bbee-6b066bedb395",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Maxime, sich so zu verhalten, dass eigene Bedürfnisse soweit wie möglich befriedigt werden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b940284a-d7c6-4365-a5c5-4c039587d593",
                                                "sense_id": "69f979bd-cb72-3536-9502-1f6d8c55f30c",
                                                "text": "„Seine Werke lehren uns viel über das Lustprinzip und die Primärvorgänge, über das Realitätsprinzip indessen – auf das die Analyse doch hinführen soll – erfahren wir verhältnismäßig wenig.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62ad0a9d-3b52-4a55-aaf1-ad1ed3441aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "69f979bd-cb72-3536-9502-1f6d8c55f30c",
                                                "text": "„Erschöpft von seinem gedrängten Tagespensum zwischen Ödipuskomplex, Analerotik, Libido und Lustprinzip kehrt Sigmund Freud nach Mitternacht in sein eheliches Schlafzimmer ein."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "848eafa4-e1e7-4278-8b11-40a0e5f92375",
                        "source_entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "jouissance",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jouissance",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea4eb75a-f17f-3de1-a48b-540d81a50a67",
                                        "entry_id": "339c8f59-5fa8-3bc4-b18b-d3e0b7fa8d49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Enjoyment, delight, pleasure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2ad2d20-f162-48e6-aa48-a716a8cd3440",
                                                "sense_id": "ea4eb75a-f17f-3de1-a48b-540d81a50a67",
                                                "text": "friendship is enjoyed according as it is desired, it is neither bred, nor nourished, nor increaseth but in jovissance, as being spirituall, and the minde being refined by use and custome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab2299be-3da6-3c90-bfd7-f05e162792c6",
                                        "entry_id": "339c8f59-5fa8-3bc4-b18b-d3e0b7fa8d49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A transgressive, excessive kind of pleasure linked to the division and splitting of the subject involved."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd31a810-8f88-4453-a8cd-111807016521",
                                                "sense_id": "ab2299be-3da6-3c90-bfd7-f05e162792c6",
                                                "text": "Instead Lyotard suggests that the worker experiences jouissance, a masochistic pleasure, in the imposed ‘mad destruction’ of their body."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d2486f2c-2047-4fa5-818c-f7b810ccaed2",
                        "source_entry_id": "266117ef-a1a8-3842-abfc-dd24eb5869ed",
                        "target_lang_word": "pleasure principle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pleasure principle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "caf3bff8-d2c7-388f-b706-a02136ad999f",
                                        "entry_id": "0c97e1f6-6959-353c-8c07-8638469a1851",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The principle that human decisions and behavior are strongly motivated by the instinctual desire of the id, arising in infancy, to experience pleasure and avoid pain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "560bbd55-07b3-4c2b-8f3c-264e90c474c7",
                                                "sense_id": "caf3bff8-d2c7-388f-b706-a02136ad999f",
                                                "text": "Bork warns that America is in the grip of a radical individualism that recognizes no limit to the right of personal gratification, one for which the pleasure principle is the only principle that counts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed49efc5-dede-44c2-bbbc-f29078b731a0",
                                                "sense_id": "caf3bff8-d2c7-388f-b706-a02136ad999f",
                                                "text": "Health, too, was a consideration, though it was very much pleasure-principle health—the right to wring out every last throb of ecstasy from one's knackered organs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e00eaf72-7197-48e1-a08b-376384a52988",
                                                "sense_id": "caf3bff8-d2c7-388f-b706-a02136ad999f",
                                                "text": "They can’t seem to decide if the moral imperative is more crucial than the pleasure principle, or the other way around."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a808d21b-1b44-42a4-afa1-29c0b975894b",
                                                "sense_id": "caf3bff8-d2c7-388f-b706-a02136ad999f",
                                                "text": "The pleasure principle is, on the whole, a sound one, then: having what you like is fine so long as you don't have too much of it in one go."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
